#
# Conformance case: occurrent/change-asymmetry
# AC: YAMATO occurrent constraint (#1081) — OccurrentChangeAsymmetry.
#
# ex:E is a Closed (completed) occurrent that bears ex:F, a logic:Fluent (a
# time-varying property). A completed occurrent must not bear a Fluent, so the
# violation rule must derive violation(E, OccurrentChangeAsymmetry). The chase
# seeds only from input.nq world facts; this program mirrors the Fluent typing.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/occurrent/change-asymmetry/> .

ex:F a logic:Fluent .
